{
 "_doc": "Composite / procedural creature templates (any book): a skeleton graph in A-pose (joint positions as FRACTIONS of the height S = the skull top; the model faces +X, left = +Y, Z up) with a radius profile per bone (fractions of S), turned into ONE implicit volume (smooth-min union of tapered capsules + ellipsoids + membrane slabs) by tools/creature_sdf.py, meshed by marching cubes, rigged by heat weights on the human bone names + extra chains (neck, jaw, tail, wings) by tools/creature_sdf_bl.py. A book's creature spec (stage/characters/<slug>/creature_spec.json) names a template and overrides any value. Bones are named like the human rig (pelvis, spine, neck, head, r_clav/r_uarm/r_farm/r_hand, r_hipb/r_thigh/r_shin/r_foot) so humanoid motion drives the body; the extra chains use the creature names (neck2.., jaw, tail1.., wing_<s>_shoulder/elbow/wrist/tip/finger1-3: a bone is named by its TAIL joint).",
